 r←GetGitHubPath url;parts;bool;searchString;url2
⍝ Takes a project URL and returns a two-item vector (group repo), or an empty vector when
⍝ `url` is not a GitHub repository URL.
⍝ Only "<host>/<group>/<repo>" is accepted. Anything deeper is refused rather than trimmed:
⍝ a URL pointing into a repository's subfolder is not evidence of where its README lives.
 r←⍬
 searchString←'github.com/'
 :If ∨/bool←searchString ⍷⎕C url
     url2←((≢searchString)+¯1+bool⍳1)↓url            ⍝ Keep the original case: paths are case sensitive
     parts←{1↓¨(⍵='/')⊂⍵}'/',url2
     :If 2=≢parts
     :AndIf ∧/0<≢¨parts
         r←parts
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
